From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Kostersitz <mkostersitz@mac.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:47:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: span or move an app by pulling it up from the bottom bar
 and dropping it

Same gesture as on the stock Surface Duo: pull an app up from the bottom bar, drag it towards the hinge or the
other screen and let go. Dropped on the hinge zone it spans over both screens; dropped on the far screen it moves
there; an app that is spanned and dropped on one screen moves to it; dropped anywhere else the app stays and goes
back to where it was (a plain pull up is still the home / recents gesture).

The zone is the hinge plus about 60 dp past the far edge and about 20 dp short on the app's own side, and the
finger has to rest for up to ~0.5 s towards the edge of the zone (the rule measured on a stock Duo 1 with
injected drags). A haptic click is issued once when resting inside the zone, and logged as "DuoDrag armed".

The decision lives in the new DuoDragDrop utility and is hooked into OtherActivityInputConsumer, so it applies to
the Launcher3 touch service whichever launcher is home. The size of the whole display comes from DisplayController
because the touch service window follows the focused screen. The app is dropped by cancelling the gesture and then
launching its task by id with the task container of the target (spanned area or panel) in the launch options,
which needs the frameworks_base change that lets a running task be moved by those options.

